 here  for those of you interested in uh you  know learning from  the lessons that we obtained the first i  believe is in order for  this approach to become  really practical we need a tighter  integration between the neural  synthesizer and a symbolic solver so for  example let's work on  differentiable fat solvers and so on um  we are ourselves working on  differentiable data log and so on um  so this would enable the approach to be  even more uh  efficient uh instead of using the  symbolic solver just as a black box  another that we another thing that we  fail to do  despite trying hard is it seems to be a  waste to  not use uh hand engineered  heuristics that work well for existing  symbolic solvers for example the  indistinguishability optimization from  each solver we were not able to  incorporate this into a neural  architecture  but this is worth trying in future  and lastly there are two parts here  which are not so  systematic which is how to design the  symbolic representation  and the reward mechanism and i believe  program synthesis itself has a role to  play  in in these two  aspects okay so with that i'll stop and  i'll be happy to take  any questions thank you mayor  uh let's say we do have time for one  question  if we want to finish more lesson time  rameen uh  would you like yeah i have a question  thank you so much for the great talk so  what's what's your take on the  i was wondering like um the work of josh  tenenbaum of clever two  have you have you guys looked into those  kind of video processing with this  approach no we haven't uh  yeah because you know like clever i  think it's called cleverer too  and this is like very similar kind of um  symbolic reasoning  while for example an object is moving  inside an environment  right okay so i was wondering like  would this technique like can you extend  this technique  to those kind of scenarios like symbolic  reasoning  yes so so this is something we are  working on currently okay which is um  uh you know allowing the user to express  um you know uh more knowledge  using symbolic constraints but then  you know determining uh but keeping them  in a logic that is  amenable to uh automatic uh  differentiation so we are currently  doing this  for a logic called data log which allows  recursion  um but then doesn't have sort of the  some of the fancier aspects of say smp  solvers  cool so so yes that is something we  would like to get to eventually  but we are not there yet great thank you  thank you mayor again and with that we'd  like to  speak to our uh last but not least  speaker  kevin ellis and  mayor nicely

